---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactEmail from '../components/ContactEmail.astro';
import TalkCollection from '../components/TalkCollection.astro';
import ShortCard from '../components/ShortCard.astro';
import { featuredVideos } from '../data/videos';
import ArticleRow from '../components/ArticleRow.astro';
import { featuredArticles } from '../data/articles';
import '../styles/articles.css';
import '../styles/videos.css';
---
<Layout>
<section class="hero wrap">
<div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"/> INDEPENDENT ENGINEER · BASED IN MALTA</div><h1>Complex systems.<br/><em>Clear decisions.</em></h1><p class="intro">I help teams fix fragile integrations, inconsistent data and contention in backend systems — and modernise legacy software without unnecessary rewrites.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#work">Explore my work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#contact">Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="hero-bio">I’m Raúl — backend engineer, systems architect and founder of AR Solución Digital. <a href="#about">More about me →</a></p><div class="hero-foot mono">GO / PHP / TYPESCRIPT / SQL <span>LESS MAGIC. MORE UNDERSTANDING.</span></div></div>
<figure class="hero-portrait"><div class="portrait-frame"><img src="/images/raul-almeida-portrait.jpg" width="400" height="400" alt="Raúl Almeida, smiling, wearing a blue jacket" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"/></div><figcaption><span><strong>Raúl Almeida</strong><span>Engineer. Founder. Curious by nature.</span></span><span class="mono">MALTA / EUROPE</span></figcaption></figure>
</section>
<div class="principle-band"><div class="wrap"><span class="mono">HOW I APPROACH THE WORK</span><p>Understand the problem. <span>Make the smallest sound change.</span> Verify it.</p></div></div>
<section id="work" class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / SELECTED WORK</span><h2>Decisions, not just deliverables.</h2></div><p>A closer look at the code, the constraints,<br/>and what I chose to leave out.</p></div>
<article class="project"><div class="project-visual wallet-visual"><div class="visual-top mono"><span>TRANSACTION BOUNDARY</span><span>SQL / BACKEND</span></div><div class="transaction"><div><span class="step-number">01</span><span>Lock the account</span></div><div><span class="step-number">02</span><span>Check idempotency</span></div><div><span class="step-number">03</span><span>Apply the operation</span></div><div><span class="step-number">04</span><span>Commit together</span></div></div><p class="mono visual-caption">CORRECTNESS BEFORE CLEVERNESS.</p></div><div class="project-copy"><span class="eyebrow">BACKEND ENGINEERING · TECHNICAL ASSIGNMENT</span><h3>A wallet that takes<br/>consistency seriously.</h3><p>Deposits, withdrawals and retries turn a small API into a useful test of engineering judgement. The interesting part is what happens when requests compete.</p><div class="tags"><span>PHP</span><span>MySQL</span><span>Idempotency</span></div><p class="project-decision"><strong>Decision:</strong> Lock the account and commit the balance change with its operation record.</p><p class="project-limit"><strong>Boundary:</strong> A technical assignment, not a live banking product.</p><details><summary>Read the concurrency decisions <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Lock the account row within the transaction, then check the idempotency key. Keep the balance change and the operation record in the same transaction. The repository contains the implementation and its tests; this is a technical assignment, not a live banking product.</p></details><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/raulalmeidatarazona/wallet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the repository ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="project reverse"><div class="project-visual media-visual"><div class="visual-top mono"><span>MEDIA SIGNAL SERVICE</span><span>CONTENT → CONTEXT</span></div><div class="article-sample"><span class="mono">UNTRUSTED INPUT</span><div class="sample-line long"></div><div class="sample-line"></div><div class="sample-line short"></div></div><div class="media-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="signal-output"><span>Searchable articles</span><span>Enrichment</span><span>Trends</span></div><p class="mono visual-caption">USEFUL OUTPUT. EXPLICIT LIMITS.</p></div><div class="project-copy"><span class="eyebrow">FULL-STACK ENGINEERING · TECHNICAL ASSIGNMENT</span><h3>From news articles<br/>to useful signals.</h3><p>A small media intelligence service exploring boolean search, LLM enrichment and time-based aggregates — without treating a model response as a source of truth.</p><div class="tags"><span>TypeScript</span><span>NestJS</span><span>React</span><span>PostgreSQL</span></div><p class="project-decision"><strong>Decision:</strong> Separate domain rules from infrastructure and make model failures explicit.</p><p class="project-limit"><strong>Boundary:</strong> Model-generated enrichment can be wrong; it is not verified fact.</p><details><summary>Read the enrichment trade-offs <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Define the API contract, separate domain rules from infrastructure, and make model cost and failure modes explicit. This assignment includes the reasoning and development transcript alongside the code.</p></details><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/raulalmeidatarazona/carma-challenge" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the repository ↗</a></div></article>
</section>
<section id="notes" class="notes-section"><div class="wrap section">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / FIELD NOTES</span><h2>Things worth understanding.</h2></div><p>Published explanations. Concrete problems.<br/>No architecture for architecture’s sake.</p></div>
  <div class="notes-toolbar"><p class="mono">SELECTED WRITING / ORIGINAL EDITIONS</p><a class="text-link" href="/notes/">All six articles →</a></div>
  <div class="notes-list">{featuredArticles.map((article, index) => <ArticleRow article={article} index={index} />)}</div>
  <div class="video-note"><span class="mono">READ / FOLLOW</span><p>From triggers and outbox to idempotent consumers: a four-part series on evolving legacy integrations.</p><a class="text-link" href="/notes/#legacy-to-events">Follow the reading path →</a></div>
</div></section>
<section id="videos" class="section wrap short-videos-section">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / SHORT VIDEOS</span><h2>Small explanations.<br/>Decisions that matter.</h2></div><p>Real business friction, explained through engineering.<br/>Original audio in Spanish. Watch without leaving the page.</p></div>
  <p class="media-privacy">The external player loads only when you press play. You can also open the original source.</p>
  <div class="featured-short">{featuredVideos.slice(0, 1).map(video => <ShortCard video={video} />)}</div>
  <div class="collection-link"><p>Part of <em>Technical decisions for growing businesses</em> — six short videos, arranged as a suggested watching path.</p><a class="text-link" href="/videos/">Explore all six videos <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</section>
<section id="talks" class="section wrap talks-section">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / TALKS & CONVERSATIONS</span><h2>Ideas are better<br/>when you share them.</h2></div><p>On stage and in conversation. <br/>Watch here, or go straight to the source.</p></div>
  <p class="media-privacy">The external player loads only when you press play. You can also open the original source.</p>
  <TalkCollection featured />
  <div class="collection-link"><a class="text-link" href="/talks/">Explore all three talks →</a></div>
</section>
<section id="about" class="section wrap about"><div><span class="eyebrow">05 / THE PERSON BEHIND THE CODE</span><h2>Hi, I’m Raúl.<br/><em>I like making things<br/>make sense.</em></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="large-copy">A backend engineer and systems architect, based in Malta. My work lives where software meets operational reality.</p><p>That means integrations that need to survive retries, databases under contention, and established systems that need to evolve without a rewrite.</p><p>I work with Go, PHP, TypeScript and SQL. Through AR Solución Digital, I also help teams understand technical problems before committing to expensive changes.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://arsoluciondigital.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">About AR Solución Digital ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="contact" class="contact-section"><div class="wrap contact"><div><span class="eyebrow">HAVE A SYSTEM WORTH THINKING ABOUT?</span><h2>Let’s start with<br/><em>the real problem.</em></h2></div><div><p>Tell me what is failing, what needs to change, or which engineering role or collaboration you have in mind.</p><a class="button light" href="mailto:raul.almeida@arsoluciondigital.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><ContactEmail /></div></div></section>
</Layout>
